+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-2)** — plan for WP-BLD-C: deterministic G07 controls in the canonical gate (`badf-build` → `VALIDATED`)\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 4 prototype → 5 workflow-integration: the controls run on every G07 dossier the gate judges.\n- **Decision:** Continue — rung C of the operator-authorized ladder (#188).\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a `scripts/badf_build.py` or a control that trusts a declaration instead of opening an artifact. Refused (BLD-I18): every control below is a `badf_gate.py` check on a typed G07 binding BLD-B already produces, or on the Work Package fields WP-IMP-B already declares; nothing new is declared to satisfy a control.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 7 build; G08 untouched.\n\n## Observed (what BLD-B made measurable, and what is still unenforced)\nOn `main` after #193, every self-produced G07 object carries an exact typed binding, and the gate refuses a malformed or artifact-disagreeing binding. Nothing yet **judges** the binding against the Work Package's contract: a request can be assembled with no human authorization on its demand; a binding's `base_sha` is not held to the WP's `base_revision`; a PASS dossier may still pass with `unexpected_paths` non-empty; a WP that declares `test_obligations` with a red phase passes without `red.observed`; a unit-test `PASS` needs no fresh composed run; the ledger's attempts are not held to `execution_budget`; a delegation may exceed the WP's surface. Those are BLD-I03/I02/I04/I07-I08/I09/I11-I13/I10 — frozen at A, producible since B, enforced at C.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0099 / BADF-DEM-0086) — seven controls, each failing-first and mutation-killed\n- **BLD-C1 authority before mutation (BLD-I03):** `self-dossier` refuses to assemble unless the WP's demand record exists with `status: AUTHORIZED` and a **human** `authorized_by`; on a PASS dossier the rule refuses evidence whose WP demand is not so authorized. Message names the demand.\n- **BLD-C2 exact baseline (BLD-I02